properties.statement:
reflow2 serves a skill for designing an argument:
- cases or situations as given;
- principles as chosen foundations;
- each position derived from a principle;
- objections aimed at what they attack (claim, premise or step) and replies;
- rival positions kept as an open dispute, never drawn as a one-way CONTRADICTS that refutes one side;
- a read-back per question.
It agrees with the tools, and find_skills finds it from "argument", "line of reasoning" or "for and against".
MEASURED 2026-10-19 in the trolley trial: no served skill covers this. design-a-proof says it is "Not for an argument for and against a choice (that is a Decision)", so the designer followed it anyway. In the cogito AI branch, a chat that read no skill drew rival verdicts as one CONTRADICTS, and one side silently read refuted.
